# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out native on
# Windows. This is not cosmetic here: infra/initdb/01-roles.sh and the Dockerfile
# entrypoints run inside Linux containers, and a CRLF shell script fails there with
# `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` - an error that names neither the file nor the cause.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything that must stay LF even if a tool decides otherwise.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
